4) Implementation: helpers for missing-annotation fixes
- File src/rules/helpers/require-story-helpers.ts implements REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE:
  const STORY_PATH = "docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md";
  const ANNOTATION = `/** @story ${STORY_PATH} */`;

- Auto-fix reporting for functions:
  function reportMissing(context, sourceCode, node, passedTarget?) {
    ...
    context.report({
      node: nameNode,
      messageId: "missingStory",
      data: { name, functionName: name },
      fix: createAddStoryFix(resolvedTarget),
      suggest: [
        {
          desc: `Add JSDoc @story annotation for function '${name}', e.g., ${ANNOTATION}`,
          fix: createAddStoryFix(resolvedTarget),
        },
      ],
    });
  }

- Auto-fix reporting for methods:
  function reportMethod(context, sourceCode, node, passedTarget?) {
    ...
    context.report({
      node: nameNode,
      messageId: "missingStory",
      data: { name, functionName: name },
      fix: createMethodFix(resolvedTarget),
      suggest: [
        {
          desc: `Add JSDoc @story annotation for function '${name}', e.g., ${ANNOTATION}`,
          fix: createMethodFix(resolvedTarget),
        },
      ],
    });
  }

- File src/rules/helpers/require-story-core.ts provides the actual fixers and ensures they are non-destructive:
  export function createAddStoryFix(target: any) {
    function addStoryFixer(fixer: any) {
      const start = ...; // computed from node ranges, no code body changes
      return fixer.insertTextBeforeRange([start, start], `${ANNOTATION}\n`);
    }
    return addStoryFixer;
  }

  export function createMethodFix(node: any) {
    function methodFixer(fixer: any) {
      const start = ...;
      return fixer.insertTextBeforeRange([start, start], `${ANNOTATION}\n  `);
    }
    return methodFixer;
  }

- These fixers only insert comments before nodes; they do not modify function bodies or logic, satisfying safety and formatting preservation constraints.

5) Implementation: valid-annotation-format rule (format auto-fix)
- File src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts exists and references this story:
  /**
   * Rule to validate @story and @req annotation format and syntax. When run with
   * ESLint's `--fix` option, this rule performs only safe @story path suffix
   * normalization ... in line with Story 008.0.
   *
   * @story docs/stories/005.0-DEV-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION.story.md
   * @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md
   * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT ...
   * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE ...
   */

- Rule meta marks it fixable and documents the safe scope of fixes:
  meta: {
    ...
    fixable: "code",
    /**
     * This rule's fixable support is limited to safe @story path suffix normalization per Story 008.0.
     * Fixes are limited strictly to adjusting the suffix portion of the @story path ...
     *
     * @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md
     * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE
     * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE
     */
  }

- Safe suffix-normalization logic (REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE):
  function getFixedStoryPath(original: string): string | null {
    if (original.includes("..")) {
      return null; // avoids unsafe or ambiguous paths
    }
    if (/\.story\.md$/.test(original)) {
      return null; // already correct
    }
    if (/\.story$/.test(original)) {
      return `${original}.md`;
    }
    if (/\.md$/.test(original)) {
      return original.replace(/\.md$/, ".story.md");
    }
    return `${original}.story.md`;
  }

- Fix application targets only the path substring and preserves surrounding formatting:
  function reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix(context, comment, collapsed, fixed) {
    const sourceCode = context.getSourceCode();
    const commentText = sourceCode.getText(comment);
    const search = "@story";
    const tagIndex = commentText.indexOf(search);
    if (tagIndex === TAG_NOT_FOUND_INDEX) { reportInvalidStoryFormat(...); return; }
    ...
    const fixRange: [number, number] = [ start + valueStartInComment, start + valueEndInComment ];

    context.report({
      node: comment as any,
      messageId: "invalidStoryFormat",
      data: { details: buildStoryErrorMessage("invalid", collapsed) },
      fix(fixer: any) {
        return fixer.replaceTextRange(fixRange, fixed);
      },
    });
  }

- Validation logic ensures fixes are only applied when safe:
  - validateStoryAnnotation(...):
    * If path already matches strict pattern, returns with no error/fix.
    * If whitespace issues exist in the raw text, it reports error without fix.
    * Else computes `fixed = getFixedStoryPath(collapsed)`; only when `fixed` also matches the strict pattern does it call reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix with a fix. Otherwise it calls reportInvalidStoryFormat without a fix.

6) Documentation of auto-fix behavior
- File user-docs/api-reference.md documents auto-fix for both relevant rules:

  For traceability/require-story-annotation:
  - "When run with `--fix`, the rule inserts a single-line placeholder JSDoc `@story` annotation above missing functions, methods, TypeScript declare functions, and interface method signatures using a built-in template aligned with Story 008.0. This template is currently fixed but structured for future configurability, and fixes are strictly limited to adding this placeholder annotation without altering the function body or changing any runtime behavior. Selective enabling of different auto-fix behaviors ... is planned for a future version."

  For traceability/valid-annotation-format:
  - "When run with `--fix`, the rule limits changes to safe `@story` path suffix normalization only—for example, adding `.md` when the path ends with `.story`, or adding `.story.md` when the base path has no extension—using targeted replacements implemented in the `getFixedStoryPath` and `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix` helpers. It does not change directories, infer new story names, or modify any surrounding comment text or whitespace, in line with Story 008.0; more advanced path normalization strategies and selective toggles ... are not yet implemented."

- These docs explicitly call out the current iteration’s capabilities and the fact that configurable templates and selective auto-fix toggling are future work, matching the story’s own notes.

